{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"33ae652f9199f0781d5d5e5df912695ef1f31e85"},"timestamp":1542675672,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzODI0NTUxOTM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3000","origin":"github"},"title":"Error: type object got multiple values for keyword argument 'name'","message":"#### What is the problem?\nTrying to create a sibling dataset on TACC, in a folder that will be publically visible on the web. The idea is to host preprocessed (fmriprep) datasets for neuroscout on there. \n\n`datalad create-sibling -s test delavega@ls5.tacc.utexas.edu:/corral-repl/utexas/neuroscout/neuroscout-data/SherlockMerlin --as-common-datasrc tacc`\n\nThe following error occurs during the process:\n```\n[INFO   ] Connecting ... \n[INFO   ] Considering to create a target dataset /home/alejandro/datasets/neuroscout-datasets/SherlockMerlin at /corral-repl/utexas/neuroscout/neuroscout-datasets/SherlockMerlin of ls5.tacc.utexas.edu \n[INFO   ] Fetching updates for \u003cDataset path=/home/alejandro/datasets/neuroscout-datasets/SherlockMerlin\u003e \n[ERROR  ] type object got multiple values for keyword argument 'name' [siblings.py:_configure_remote:543] (TypeError)\n```\n\nIt seems to work without the `--as-common-datasrc` argument. I'm assuming this is necessary for others to be able to do `datalad install` with this dataset. The plan was to also add a remote-url (once the web server is turned on), and publish to github. \n\n#### What version of DataLad are you using (run `datalad --version`)? On what operating system (consider running `datalad wtf`)?\n0.11.0 (on workstation)\n0.11.0 (on TACC, installed through conda, due to lack of admin)","files":null}]}